within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.J_AntiinfectivesForSystemicUse.J01C_BetaLactamAntibacterialsPenicillins.J01CG01_Sulbactam;
model Sulbactam_Yokoyama2014_PD_killing_effect_of_sulbactam_log_10
  "sigmoid_emax exposure-response sweep — Yokoyama_2014 :: killing effect of sulbactam (log 10 CFU of the A. baumannii per thigh or lung at 24 h) (killing effect of sulbactam (log 10 CFU of the A. baumannii per thigh or lung at 24 h))"
  extends Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep(
    E0 = 0.52,      // [log 10 CFU/Organ]
    Emax = -5.19,  // [log 10 CFU/Organ]
    EC50 = 0.446,  // [1; % × 0.01]
    gamma = 2.93,
    exposure_per_s = 0.01);   // 1 % per second
  // imax_as_negative_emax: Imax (Q323) enters SigmoidEmaxSweep as −Emax
  annotation(experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 450, Interval = 0.9),
    Documentation(info = "<html><body><h4>Sulbactam_Yokoyama2014_PD_killing_effect_of_sulbactam_log_10</h4><p>The steady-state exposure-response curve of Yokoyama Y et al., <i>International journal of antimicrobial agents 43(6):547–552</i> 2014 (<a href=\"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ijantimicag.2014.02.012\">doi:10.1016/j.ijantimicag.2014.02.012</a>) — killing effect of sulbactam (log 10 CFU of the A. baumannii per thigh or lung at 24 h) [log 10 CFU/thigh] against sulbactam % — obtained by sweeping the driver instead of simulating a dose. Model family: sigmoid_emax.</p><h4>The parameters, in the paper's terms</h4><pre>  E0    =       0.52 log 10 CFU/Organ drug-free response (baseline) (E 0, Q324)
  Emax  =       5.19 log 10 CFU/Organ maximal effect term (E max, Q323)
  EC50  =       44.6 %        exposure at half of the maximal effect term (EC 50, Q321)
  gamma =       2.93          Hill coefficient (γ, Q325)</pre><p>The algebra is <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Pharmacodynamic.SigmoidEmaxSweep\">SigmoidEmaxSweep</a>; this model only supplies the numbers. The x axis is one % of sulbactam per second of simulated time: there is no state, no dose and no kinetics — plot <code>response</code> against <code>exposure</code> (or <code>time</code>).</p><h4>What it reproduces</h4><pre>  exposure = 0         response 0.52   (drug-free)
  exposure = EC50 (44.6 %)  response -2.075
  exposure -> infinity  response -4.67</pre></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>11/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from Yokoyama_2014: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: curated candidate</li></ul></body></html>"));
end Sulbactam_Yokoyama2014_PD_killing_effect_of_sulbactam_log_10;
